 record here runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids August to September came in under 90% of normal in 37 of 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 that middle ran 20% of normal in January to February and 41% in September to October. Every grid had its driest year in 1988, with grid 26856 at 56% that year. A preliminary estimate for grid 26858 puts August to September 2026 at 163.0, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
